    "input": "search_document: Good morning! I understand the urgency of your situation. Based on the handbook excerpts provided, here is the information regarding your request to upgrade your shipping method.\n\n**Regarding the $15.00 Upgrade Fee**\nThe handbook states that upgrading your shipping method from Standard to Express incurs an additional fee of $15.00 [order_changes.3]. However, the provided excerpts **do not contain specific instructions on how to apply this upgrade to an existing order** (e.g., whether to do it via the website, by phone, or if it is possible after the order has already been processed).\n\n**Clarification on the \"Contradiction\"**\nYou mentioned confusion regarding the downgrade refund range of $5.00\u2013$12.00. This is not contradictory to the upgrade fee. The handbook explains that the $15.00 upgrade fee is calculated based on the difference in carrier rates [order_changes.3]. Conversely, if you were to *downgrade* from Express to Standard, you would receive a refund of the difference, which is typically between $5.00 and $12.00 [order_changes.3]. These are two separate actions with different financial impacts.\n\n**Important Timing Constraint**\nPlease note that order details, including shipping methods, can generally be modified up to 24 hours after placing the order [order_changes.1]. If your order is still within this 24-hour window, you may be able to make the change. If the order has already been locked or processed, the handbook does not specify a procedure for changing shipping methods at that stage.\n\n**Next Steps**\nSince the handbook excerpts do not provide the specific steps to execute this upgrade on your live order, and given the time sensitivity of your request, I recommend escalating this ticket to a human agent immediately. They can check the status of your order and apply the $15.00 Express shipping upgrade if it is still possible.\n\nWould you like me to escalate this to a human agent for immediate assistance?",
